Demo corpus: simple_topic_modeling/data/demo_corpus.csv

    Content: 295 articles from two Swiss newspapers of 1914, the "Journal de
             Genève" and the "Gazette de Lausanne". The file keeps the first
             250 words of each article, the publication date, and the section
             heading that the newspaper printed above it.

    Source:  Le Temps Historical Archive (https://www.letempsarchives.ch/),
             digitised and published by the Digital Humanities Laboratory of
             the EPFL for the 2015 Swiss Open Cultural Data Hackathon.
             Project page: https://hack.glam.opendata.ch/project/234
             Compiled by: Yannick Rochat and Giovanni Colavizza, EPFL DHLab.

    License: Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0), as
             stated by the publishers of the archive.

    Status:  The articles are anonymous newspaper text, published in 1914.
             Swiss law releases an anonymous work 70 years after publication,
             so the articles left copyright in 1985. A faithful scan of a
             public-domain text creates no new right in Switzerland. The CC
             BY 4.0 grant covers the digitisation, and this notice gives the
             attribution that the grant asks for.

    Build:   scripts/build_demo_corpus.py rebuilds the file from the archive.
             It records each source URL and each SHA-256 in
             scripts/demo_corpus.provenance.json.

Demo text: simple_topic_modeling/data/demo_text.txt

    Content: Mary Wollstonecraft, "A Vindication of the Rights of Woman:
             with Strictures on Political and Moral Subjects", first
             published in London in 1792. The file holds one paragraph per
             line. It leaves out the table of contents and the bare chapter
             and section numbers. It keeps each chapter title and each
             sentence of the work. It also leaves out the anonymous
             biographical sketch that the Project Gutenberg edition prints
             before the work, because the sketch has no author and no date.

    Source:  Project Gutenberg, eBook #3420
             (https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/3420).
             File: https://www.gutenberg.org/cache/epub/3420/pg3420.txt

    Author:  Mary Wollstonecraft (1759-1797).

    Status:  Public domain worldwide. The author died in 1797, so the term
             of protection ended long ago in every country. The build script
             removes the Project Gutenberg header, footer, and licence, and
             the "Project Gutenberg" trademark with them. Only the public
             domain work remains, so the Project Gutenberg licence does not
             apply to this file.

    Build:   scripts/build_demo_text.py rebuilds the file from the source. It
             records the source URL and each SHA-256 in
             scripts/demo_text.provenance.json.

